<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Schenectady, New York</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Schenectady is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> State on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohawk-river">Mohawk River</a>, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> settlers in 1661. On the night of 8–9 February 1690, during King William's War, a French and Native raiding party from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montreal">Montreal</a> surprised and burned the village, killing about 60 people. It later grew into an industrial city, the home of the General Electric company.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/schenectady-new-york.jpg" alt="Schenectady, New York" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: UpstateNYer · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nott_SE_Landscape.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
